<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Undo Redo LLD" id="undoredo">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1434" dy="844" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1920" pageHeight="1400">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        
        <!-- Title -->
        <mxCell id="title" value="UNDO / REDO FEATURE - Command Design Pattern (Request Encapsulation &amp; Reversibility)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1840" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SECTION 1-3: CLASS DIAGRAM -->
        <mxCell id="subtitle1" value="SECTION 1-3: CLASS DIAGRAM (Command Pattern - Turn Request into Objects)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="70" width="1000" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Receiver -->
        <mxCell id="receiver_class" value="RECEIVER: AirConditioner&#xa;&#xa;- isOn: boolean&#xa;- temperature: int&#xa;&#xa;+ turnOn(): void&#xa;  // isOn = true&#xa;  // Print: 'AC is ON'&#xa;&#xa;+ turnOff(): void&#xa;  // isOn = false&#xa;  // Print: 'AC is OFF'&#xa;&#xa;+ setTemperature(temp): void&#xa;  // temperature = temp&#xa;  // Print: 'Temp set to {temp}'" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="120" width="300" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Command Interface -->
        <mxCell id="command_interface" value="&lt;&lt;interface&gt;&gt;&#xa;ICommand&#xa;&#xa;+ execute(): void&#xa;+ undo(): void" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="380" y="120" width="200" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- TurnOnCommand -->
        <mxCell id="turnon_command" value="TurnACOnCommand&#xa;(implements ICommand)&#xa;&#xa;- ac: AirConditioner&#xa;&#xa;+ TurnACOnCommand(ac)&#xa;  // this.ac = ac&#xa;&#xa;+ execute(): void&#xa;  // ac.turnOn()&#xa;&#xa;+ undo(): void&#xa;  // ac.turnOff()  // REVERSE!" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="120" width="280" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- TurnOffCommand -->
        <mxCell id="turnoff_command" value="TurnACOffCommand&#xa;(implements ICommand)&#xa;&#xa;- ac: AirConditioner&#xa;&#xa;+ TurnACOffCommand(ac)&#xa;&#xa;+ execute(): void&#xa;  // ac.turnOff()&#xa;&#xa;+ undo(): void&#xa;  // ac.turnOn()  // REVERSE!" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="940" y="120" width="280" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SetTempCommand -->
        <mxCell id="settemp_command" value="SetTemperatureCommand&#xa;(implements ICommand)&#xa;&#xa;- ac: AirConditioner&#xa;- newTemp: int&#xa;- prevTemp: int  // For undo!&#xa;&#xa;+ SetTemperatureCommand(ac, temp)&#xa;&#xa;+ execute(): void&#xa;  // prevTemp = ac.getTemperature()&#xa;  // ac.setTemperature(newTemp)&#xa;&#xa;+ undo(): void&#xa;  // ac.setTemperature(prevTemp)" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1260" y="120" width="320" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Invoker -->
        <mxCell id="invoker_class" value="INVOKER: RemoteControl&#xa;&#xa;- command: ICommand  // Current button&#xa;- commandHistory: Stack&lt;ICommand&gt;&#xa;  // For undo/redo&#xa;&#xa;+ setCommand(ICommand cmd)&#xa;  // command = cmd&#xa;&#xa;+ pressButton(): void&#xa;  // command.execute()&#xa;  // commandHistory.push(command)&#xa;  // Client just presses button!&#xa;&#xa;+ undo(): void&#xa;  // if (!commandHistory.isEmpty()):&#xa;    // cmd = commandHistory.pop()&#xa;    // cmd.undo()&#xa;&#xa;+ redo(): void&#xa;  // (Redo stack implementation)" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1620" y="120" width="300" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Command Pattern Explanation -->
        <mxCell id="pattern_explanation" value="COMMAND PATTERN STRUCTURE:&#xa;&#xa;PROBLEM 1: LACK OF ABSTRACTION&#xa;&#xa;WITHOUT COMMAND PATTERN:&#xa;Client code:&#xa;  ac.turnOn();&#xa;  ac.setTemperature(24);&#xa;  ac.turnOff();&#xa;&#xa;Issues:&#xa;- Client knows AC internal methods (tight coupling)&#xa;- What if turnOn() requires 10 steps? Client must know all&#xa;- What if steps change? Client code breaks&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;PROBLEM 2: UNDO/REDO IMPOSSIBLE&#xa;&#xa;User: 'Undo turn on'&#xa;How? Client must remember: 'Oh, I did turnOn(), so call turnOff()'&#xa;Client tracks state? NO! That's receiver's responsibility.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;PROBLEM 3: CODE MAINTENANCE NIGHTMARE&#xa;&#xa;Add Bulb to remote:&#xa;Client now needs:&#xa;  ac.turnOn();&#xa;  bulb.turnOn();&#xa;  ac.setTemp(24);&#xa;  bulb.setBrightness(80);&#xa;&#xa;Client becomes BULKY, TIGHTLY COUPLED to all devices.&#xa;Adding device → modify client everywhere.&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;SOLUTION: COMMAND PATTERN&#xa;&#xa;Turn REQUESTS into OBJECTS (commands)&#xa;&#xa;4 PARTICIPANTS:&#xa;&#xa;1. RECEIVER (AirConditioner)&#xa;   - Dumb object, performs actions when told&#xa;   - turnOn(), turnOff(), setTemperature()&#xa;   - NO knowledge of commands or invoker&#xa;&#xa;2. COMMAND (ICommand interface)&#xa;   - Encapsulates request as object&#xa;   - execute(): perform action&#xa;   - undo(): reverse action&#xa;&#xa;3. CONCRETE COMMAND (TurnACOnCommand)&#xa;   - Implements ICommand&#xa;   - HAS-A Receiver (ac)&#xa;   - execute() calls receiver.turnOn()&#xa;   - undo() calls receiver.turnOff() (REVERSE!)&#xa;&#xa;4. INVOKER (RemoteControl)&#xa;   - Triggers commands&#xa;   - Maintains command history (Stack)&#xa;   - Client interacts ONLY with invoker&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;CLIENT CODE:&#xa;&#xa;// Setup&#xa;AirConditioner ac = new AirConditioner();&#xa;RemoteControl remote = new RemoteControl();&#xa;&#xa;// Set command (bind button)&#xa;remote.setCommand(new TurnACOnCommand(ac));&#xa;&#xa;// User action&#xa;remote.pressButton();  // Client doesn't know it calls ac.turnOn()!&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;COMMUNICATION FLOW:&#xa;&#xa;Client → Invoker → Command → Receiver&#xa;&#xa;Client: remote.pressButton()&#xa;  ↓&#xa;Invoker: command.execute()&#xa;  ↓&#xa;Command: ac.turnOn()&#xa;  ↓&#xa;Receiver: isOn = true&#xa;&#xa;Client abstracted from receiver details!&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;UNDO/REDO MECHANISM:&#xa;&#xa;COMMAND HISTORY STACK:&#xa;[TurnOnCmd, SetTempCmd, TurnOffCmd] ← top&#xa;&#xa;User clicks UNDO:&#xa;1. remote.undo()&#xa;2. cmd = commandHistory.pop()  // TurnOffCmd&#xa;3. cmd.undo()  // Calls ac.turnOn()&#xa;4. AC turns ON (reverts turnOff)&#xa;&#xa;Stack after undo:&#xa;[TurnOnCmd, SetTempCmd] ← top&#xa;&#xa;User clicks UNDO again:&#xa;1. cmd = commandHistory.pop()  // SetTempCmd&#xa;2. cmd.undo()  // Calls ac.setTemperature(prevTemp)&#xa;3. Temperature reverts&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;REDO MECHANISM (2 Stack Approach):&#xa;&#xa;commandHistory: [executed commands]&#xa;redoStack: [undone commands]&#xa;&#xa;Execute command:&#xa;  - Push to commandHistory&#xa;  - Clear redoStack (new action invalidates redo)&#xa;&#xa;Undo:&#xa;  - Pop from commandHistory&#xa;  - Execute cmd.undo()&#xa;  - Push cmd to redoStack&#xa;&#xa;Redo:&#xa;  - Pop from redoStack&#xa;  - Execute cmd.execute()&#xa;  - Push cmd to commandHistory&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;BENEFITS:&#xa;&#xa;1. DECOUPLING&#xa;   - Client doesn't know receiver&#xa;   - Receiver doesn't know command or invoker&#xa;   - Easy to change receiver implementation&#xa;&#xa;2. ABSTRACTION&#xa;   - Client: just pressButton()&#xa;   - No knowledge of AC methods&#xa;&#xa;3. UNDO/REDO BUILT-IN&#xa;   - Command has undo() method&#xa;   - Invoker manages history stack&#xa;   - Client: remote.undo() — that's it!&#xa;&#xa;4. EXTENSIBILITY&#xa;   - New command? Create new class implementing ICommand&#xa;   - No changes to existing commands/invoker/receiver&#xa;   - Open-Closed Principle&#xa;&#xa;5. MACRO COMMANDS&#xa;   - CompositeCommand with List&lt;ICommand&gt;&#xa;   - execute() calls all commands&#xa;   - undo() calls all in reverse order&#xa;   - Example: 'Party Mode' = TurnOnLights + TurnOnMusic + SetTemp(18)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;COMMAND vs STRATEGY PATTERN:&#xa;&#xa;STRATEGY:&#xa;- Algorithm selection at runtime&#xa;- Example: PaymentStrategy (UPI/Card/Cash)&#xa;- No undo/redo&#xa;- Focus: behavioral flexibility&#xa;&#xa;COMMAND:&#xa;- Request encapsulation&#xa;- Undo/redo support&#xa;- Command queuing, logging&#xa;- Focus: action reversibility" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=9;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="460" width="1000" height="1220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- Example Flow -->
        <mxCell id="example_title" value="EXAMPLE: TEXT EDITOR UNDO/REDO" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="460" width="840" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="example_flow" value="TEXT EDITOR COMMANDS:&#xa;&#xa;1. InsertTextCommand(text, position)&#xa;   execute(): insert text at position&#xa;   undo(): delete text at position&#xa;&#xa;2. DeleteTextCommand(position, length)&#xa;   execute(): delete length chars at position&#xa;   undo(): insert deletedText at position (store deleted text!)&#xa;&#xa;3. FormatTextCommand(range, boldOn)&#xa;   execute(): apply bold to range&#xa;   undo(): remove bold from range (store prev format!)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;USER ACTIONS:&#xa;&#xa;Type 'Hello'&#xa;  → InsertTextCmd('H', 0).execute()&#xa;  → InsertTextCmd('e', 1).execute()&#xa;  → InsertTextCmd('l', 2).execute()&#xa;  → InsertTextCmd('l', 3).execute()&#xa;  → InsertTextCmd('o', 4).execute()&#xa;&#xa;commandHistory: [Insert(H), Insert(e), Insert(l), Insert(l), Insert(o)]&#xa;Document: 'Hello'&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;User presses Ctrl+Z (Undo):&#xa;  → cmd = pop()  // Insert(o)&#xa;  → cmd.undo()  // Delete 'o' at position 4&#xa;  → redoStack.push(cmd)&#xa;&#xa;commandHistory: [Insert(H), Insert(e), Insert(l), Insert(l)]&#xa;redoStack: [Insert(o)]&#xa;Document: 'Hell'&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;User presses Ctrl+Z again:&#xa;  → cmd = pop()  // Insert(l)&#xa;  → cmd.undo()&#xa;&#xa;commandHistory: [Insert(H), Insert(e), Insert(l)]&#xa;redoStack: [Insert(o), Insert(l)]&#xa;Document: 'Hel'&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;User presses Ctrl+Y (Redo):&#xa;  → cmd = redoStack.pop()  // Insert(l)&#xa;  → cmd.execute()  // Re-insert 'l' at position 3&#xa;  → commandHistory.push(cmd)&#xa;&#xa;commandHistory: [Insert(H), Insert(e), Insert(l), Insert(l)]&#xa;redoStack: [Insert(o)]&#xa;Document: 'Hell'&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;User types 'p' (new action):&#xa;  → InsertTextCmd('p', 4).execute()&#xa;  → redoStack.clear()  // NEW action invalidates redo!&#xa;&#xa;commandHistory: [Insert(H), Insert(e), Insert(l), Insert(l), Insert(p)]&#xa;redoStack: []&#xa;Document: 'Hellp'&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;COMPLEX EXAMPLE: FORMAT CHANGE&#xa;&#xa;Document: 'Hello World'&#xa;User selects 'Hello', makes it bold&#xa;  → FormatCmd(range(0,5), bold=true).execute()&#xa;  → Store: prevFormat = {bold: false}&#xa;&#xa;Document: **Hello** World&#xa;commandHistory: [..., Format(0-5, bold)]&#xa;&#xa;Undo:&#xa;  → cmd = pop()  // FormatCmd&#xa;  → cmd.undo()  // Apply prevFormat {bold: false}&#xa;&#xa;Document: Hello World  (back to normal)&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;MACRO COMMAND EXAMPLE:&#xa;&#xa;class MacroCommand implements ICommand {&#xa;  List&lt;ICommand&gt; commands;&#xa;  &#xa;  void execute() {&#xa;    for (ICommand cmd : commands) {&#xa;      cmd.execute();&#xa;    }&#xa;  }&#xa;  &#xa;  void undo() {&#xa;    // Reverse order!&#xa;    for (int i = commands.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {&#xa;      commands.get(i).undo();&#xa;    }&#xa;  }&#xa;}&#xa;&#xa;Macro: 'Format as Heading'&#xa;  = [SelectLineCmd, BoldCmd, IncreaseFontSizeCmd(14), ColorCmd(blue)]&#xa;&#xa;Execute macro: all 4 commands run&#xa;Undo macro: all 4 commands undo in REVERSE order&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;IMPLEMENTATION TIPS:&#xa;&#xa;1. STORE STATE FOR UNDO&#xa;   - DeleteTextCmd: store deletedText&#xa;   - SetTemperatureCmd: store prevTemp&#xa;   - FormatCmd: store prevFormat&#xa;   - Otherwise, undo impossible!&#xa;&#xa;2. COMMAND EXECUTION ORDERING&#xa;   - commandHistory.push() AFTER execute() succeeds&#xa;   - If execute() fails, don't push to history&#xa;   - Undo only successful commands&#xa;&#xa;3. REDO STACK CLEARING&#xa;   - Any NEW command → redoStack.clear()&#xa;   - Redo only valid if no new actions after undo&#xa;&#xa;4. MEMORY MANAGEMENT&#xa;   - Limit commandHistory size (e.g., 100 undos)&#xa;   - If full, remove oldest: commandHistory.removeFirst()&#xa;&#xa;5. SERIALIZATION&#xa;   - Save commandHistory to disk&#xa;   - Replay on app restart → restore document state&#xa;   - Command sourcing / Event sourcing pattern&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;OTHER USE CASES:&#xa;&#xa;1. JOB QUEUES&#xa;   - Commands queued for execution&#xa;   - Worker pulls command from queue&#xa;   - Retry on failure (cmd.execute())&#xa;&#xa;2. TRANSACTION LOGGING&#xa;   - Database transactions as commands&#xa;   - execute() = commit&#xa;   - undo() = rollback&#xa;&#xa;3. NETWORK PROTOCOLS&#xa;   - HTTP requests as commands&#xa;   - Retry, replay, log&#xa;&#xa;4. GAME REPLAYS&#xa;   - Player actions as commands&#xa;   - Replay game by re-executing commands&#xa;   - Undo to previous game state&#xa;&#xa;5. BROWSER BACK/FORWARD&#xa;   - Navigation as commands&#xa;   - Back = undo (go to prev URL)&#xa;   - Forward = redo (go to next URL)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=9;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="500" width="840" height="1680" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SECTION 4: ER DIAGRAM -->
        <mxCell id="title_er" value="SECTION 4: ER DIAGRAM" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1720" width="1000" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="er_device" value="Device (Receiver)&#xa;&#xa;PK  deviceId: INT&#xa;    deviceName: VARCHAR(100)&#xa;    deviceType: VARCHAR(50)&#xa;    currentState: JSON" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=left;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1780" width="220" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="er_command" value="Command&#xa;&#xa;PK  commandId: INT&#xa;    commandType: VARCHAR(50)&#xa;    commandData: JSON&#xa;    createdAt: DATETIME" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=left;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="300" y="1780" width="220" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="er_execution" value="CommandExecution&#xa;&#xa;PK  executionId: INT&#xa;FK  deviceId: INT&#xa;FK  commandId: INT&#xa;    executedAt: DATETIME&#xa;    executionStatus: ENUM&#xa;    prevState: JSON  // For undo" style="swimlane;fontStyle=1;align=left;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="1780" width="240" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <!-- SECTION 7: SCENARIO QUESTIONS -->
        <mxCell id="title_scenario" value="SECTION 7: SCENARIO QUESTIONS" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1980" width="1000" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
        <mxCell id="scenario" value="Q1: Command history stack grows indefinitely. Memory issue. How to limit?&#xa;A1: Limit stack size (e.g., 100 commands). When full, remove oldest: if (commandHistory.size() > 100) commandHistory.removeFirst(). Alternatively, compress old commands (group similar commands: 100 InsertChar → InsertString). Persist to disk for infinite undo, load on demand (event sourcing).&#xa;&#xa;Q2: Multiple users editing same document (Google Docs). How to handle collaborative undo?&#xa;A2: Operational Transformation (OT) or CRDT. Each user has own command stack. Broadcast commands to all users. OT transforms concurrent commands to maintain consistency. Example: User1 inserts 'A' at pos 0, User2 inserts 'B' at pos 0 → OT adjusts positions. Undo only own commands (filter commandHistory by userId).&#xa;&#xa;Q3: Command execution fails (network error during save). Undo behavior?&#xa;A3: Only push to commandHistory if execute() succeeds. Pattern: boolean execute() returns success/fail. If fail, don't add to history, show error, no undo needed. Transactional semantics: either full success or rollback (try-catch, on exception call undo() immediately, don't push to stack).&#xa;&#xa;Q4: Redo stack invalidated by new action. Why?&#xa;A4: Redo assumes future = undone past. New action creates new future, old redo path invalid. Example: Type 'ABC', undo 'C' (redo = ['C']), type 'D' → document now 'ABD'. Redoing 'C' makes no sense (would give 'ABDC'?). Solution: clear redoStack on any new command except redo itself.&#xa;&#xa;Q5: How to implement unlimited undo/redo across app restarts?&#xa;A5: Event Sourcing: persist all commands to durable storage (DB, log file). On app start, replay all commands to restore state. commandHistory loaded from storage. Undo/redo operates on persistent log. Benefits: full audit trail, time travel (restore to any point), disaster recovery. Trade-off: storage cost, replay time for large history." style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Courier New;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2040" width="1000" height="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
